I left out the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-rw`, so it has no filesystem access for the log file and no HTTP import for the metadata service. Adding either would exceed its authority. Operations would need to route those through a node that holds the matching capability.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;

        // Only a digest that was actually published marks its considered
        // items as seen; an unpublished run leaves the store untouched.
        if published.published {
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                state_rw::put(id.as_str(), published.date.as_str());
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

